{"ts":1788827631838,"content":"Supervisor adjudication of the R005 spiral signal on Step 3: NOT circling — every round has closed its findings and R005 raises two new, legitimate classes. Implement both, then request R006:\n\n1. Packet location in doRatifyGate: resolve reviewsDir/statusPath with the SAME packetRepoId/packetTaskPath logic buildExecutionUnit uses (execution.ts ~2548) — extract a shared helper rather than duplicating it — and bind the worktree to the cited hold's laneNumber/segment, not task.laneNumber alone. Add one cross-repo-segment regression for the trusted operation.\n\n2. collectChangedPaths must FAIL CLOSED: if either git probe (diff --name-only HEAD / ls-files --others) fails, return a failure (or throw) and have BOTH issuance and finalize refuse with a diagnostic naming the probe. Add injected probe-failure tests for both callers.\n\nScope guard: if R006 raises findings of a NEW class again (not regressions of 1–2), do not start a fifth implementation round — log them as a blocker in STATUS.md with the finding text, then escalate_to_supervisor with the R006 path and stop. I will rule on scope from there. Keep lint at 283 and format:check clean before requesting the review.","id":"1788827631838-a6acb","type":"steer"}
{"ts":1788828256604,"content":"Supervisor ruling on R006 scope-guard evaluation: all three findings are INCOMPLETE FIXES of R005 items (#1 cross-repo counter path, #2 cited-hold lane fallback), plus a format gate — not a new class. So this is in scope: fix them and request R007. Specifically: (1) allocate the R number from statusPathForCounter (packet-home STATUS), and add the behavioural doRatifyGate cross-repo test that asserts packet-home STATUS counter, APPROVE and JSON all update together; (2) fail closed when rulingHold.laneNumber has no lane record — no fallback to task.laneNumber — and stamp the audit entry with rulingHold.laneNumber; add the negative regression; (3) run npm run format before requesting review. The scope guard still stands for R007: a genuinely NEW class → log blocker + escalate_to_supervisor, no further round.","id":"1788828256604-522cc","type":"steer"}
{"ts":1788828856285,"content":"R007 evaluation: one finding, same R004 proof-binding class (not new scope) and the reviewer is right — a persisted symbolic ref re-resolved at finalize tracks a moved HEAD. Fix and request R008: at finalize, require the persisted revision proof to be a canonical 40-hex object id STRING-EQUAL to ctx.headRevision (no merge-base re-resolution of persisted refs; keep isAncestor only for the issuance-time check if you still need it), and reject noncanonical refs in isValidGateRatification so a hand-edited record with \"HEAD\" is refused at read. Add the behavioural regression the reviewer describes (record with a symbolic ref, later clean commit → finalize refused). This is the last item — if R008 is clean, proceed to Step 4.","id":"1788828856285-26fdc","type":"steer"}
{"ts":1788829234766,"content":"Supervisor adjudication of the round-6 spiral signal: R008's single finding is legitimate and in the R004 dirty-tree class — the blanket \".pi\" exemption lets tracked .pi/taskplane-config.json / .pi/agents/*.md drift past ratification into the merge candidate. Fix it: remove the blanket \".pi\" prefix from BOTH the issuance (ratification-op.ts) and finalize (lane-runner.ts) allow-lists; allow only genuinely runtime-owned paths that can actually appear in the lane worktree (the task packet's STATUS.md, .DONE, the .reviews/ directory of the task — and nothing else unless you can name why). Add issuance- and finalize-level regressions using a tracked .pi/taskplane-config.json edit. Then request R009.\n\nHARD CAP: R009 is the final review round for Step 3. If R009 is anything other than APPROVE, do NOT implement further — record the R009 findings verbatim in STATUS.md Blockers, then escalate_to_supervisor with: the R009 file path, the list of every class fixed in R003–R009, and your assessment of whether the remaining finding is a real fail-open or a residual-risk judgement call. Stop and wait for the ruling. Six closed rounds is enough evidence that the surface converges only by supervisor decision.","id":"1788829234766-95110","type":"steer"}
